# GOV.UK Frontend Components

## Role in Form Journeys

GOV.UK Frontend provides consistent, accessible UI components for all form journeys. Components are imported as Nunjucks macros and follow strict patterns for errors, validation, and accessibility.

## Component Patterns

### Importing Components

```njk
{% from "govuk/components/input/macro.njk" import govukInput %}
{% from "govuk/components/radios/macro.njk" import govukRadios %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/error-summary/macro.njk" import govukErrorSummary %}
{% from "govuk/components/back-link/macro.njk" import govukBackLink %}
{% from "govuk/components/summary-list/macro.njk" import govukSummaryList %}
```

### Error Summary Pattern

Always show error summary at top of form when errors exist:

```njk
{% if error %}
  {{ govukErrorSummary({
    titleText: "There is a problem",
    errorList: [{
      text: error,
      href: "#field-id"
    }]
  }) }}
{% endif %}
```

### Field-Level Errors

Use conditional syntax for error messages - NEVER use null:

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  name: "fieldName",
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error
}) }}

{# ❌ NEVER DO THIS - causes 500 errors #}
{# errorMessage: error ? { text: error } : null #}
```

### Radio Buttons

```njk
{{ govukRadios({
  name: "preference",
  fieldset: {
    legend: {
      text: heading,
      isPageHeading: true,
      classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--xl"
    }
  },
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error,
  items: [{
    value: "option1",
    text: "Option 1",
    checked: selectedValue === "option1"
  }]
}) }}
```

### Checkboxes

Checkboxes return array when multiple selected, single value when one selected. Normalize in POST controller:

```javascript
let { options } = request.payload
if (!Array.isArray(options)) {
  options = options ? [options] : []
}
```

### Summary List with Change Links

Summary page must pass entire ROUTES object (not string) from controller:

```javascript
// Controller
return h.view('journey-name/summary', {
  fieldValue: request.yar.get('field'),
  ROUTES // Pass entire object
})
```

```njk
{{ govukSummaryList({
  rows: [{
    key: { text: "Field name" },
    value: { text: fieldValue },
    actions: {
      items: [{
        href: ROUTES.FIELD_PAGE,
        text: "Change",
        visuallyHiddenText: "field name"
      }]
    }
  }]
}) }}
```

### Conditional Summary Rows

Only show relevant fields based on user choices:

```njk
{{ govukSummaryList({
  rows: [
    {
      key: { text: "Always shown" },
      value: { text: value }
    },
    {
      key: { text: "Conditional field" },
      value: { text: conditionalValue }
    } if condition === "value"
  ]
}) }}
```

### Back Link

Every page except start must have a back link:

```njk
{% block beforeContent %}
  {{ govukBackLink({
    href: backLink
  }) }}
{% endblock %}
```

Controller calculates back link (may be conditional):

```javascript
const backLink = userChoice === 'optionA' ? ROUTES.PAGE_A : ROUTES.PAGE_B
return h.view('journey-name/page', { backLink })
```

### File Upload

```njk
{{ govukFileUpload({
  id: "uploadFile",
  name: "uploadFile",
  label: {
    text: "Upload a file"
  },
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error
}) }}
```

## Common Mistakes

### Using null in Conditional Properties (500 Error)

❌ **Never use null or ternary with null:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: error ? { text: error } : null
}) }}
```

✅ **Use if expression instead:**

```njk
{{ govukInput({
  errorMessage: { text: error } if error
}) }}
```

This applies to all conditional properties: `errorMessage`, `value`, `hint`, etc.

### Missing Error Summary

Always show error summary when errors exist. Missing summary creates poor UX.

### Incorrect Form Structure

Forms must use:

- `method="post" novalidate"` (never GET for submissions)
- Proper form tags surrounding fields
- Submit button (not link) inside form

### Wrong Change Link Format

❌ Passing route as string:

```javascript
return h.view('summary', { changeLink: '/journey/page' })
```

✅ Passing entire ROUTES object:

```javascript
return h.view('summary', { ROUTES })
```

```njk
{{ govukSummaryList({
  rows: [{
    actions: {
      items: [{
        href: ROUTES.PAGE // Use from ROUTES object
      }]
    }
  }]
}) }}
```

### Missing visuallyHiddenText on Change Links

Change links must include `visuallyHiddenText` for accessibility:

```njk
{
  href: ROUTES.FIELD_PAGE,
  text: "Change",
  visuallyHiddenText: "field name" // Required!
}
```

## Known Issues

### Null Values in Macros Cause 500 Errors

**Problem**: Using `null` in conditional macro parameters causes template rendering to crash with 500 Internal Server Error.

**Root Cause**: Nunjucks doesn't handle `null` values in macro parameters properly.

**Solution**: Use if expression syntax instead of ternary with null:

```njk
errorMessage: { text: error } if error
```

**Reference**: See [nunjucks.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nunjucks.mdc) for template syntax patterns.

